{
  "requirement": "Number of hexadecimal digits in the identity hash of an anonymous selector segment.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub const HASH_DIGITS: usize = 12;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.outlines.HASH_DIGITS` declares one constant, `pub const HASH_DIGITS: usize = 12`. It is the number of hex digits in the identity hash of an anonymous selector segment.\n\n- **Constant value.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors]` asserts `HASH_DIGITS == 12`. The constant is imported from `outline::selector`.\n- **Digit count in real anonymous segments.** The same test checks every anonymous `line@…` selector that plain-text outlining produces. Each prefix after `line@` has length `HASH_DIGITS` and consists only of ASCII hex digits. Each prefix also equals the first 12 characters of `structural_hash`.\n- **Other anonymous segments.** The tree-sitter builder `Builder::finish` and `markdown.rs#fn[parse]` slice their hashes with `[..HASH_DIGITS]`. They use the same constant directly, with no conditional or transformation of their own. The value assertion and the plain-text check therefore cover them.\n- **`public_exports_match_the_appendix`** in `public_api.rs` is marked as a test for the public API. It adds nothing specific to this requirement and is not needed for it.\n\nA wrong value or a wrong digit count would fail these assertions, so I found no gap.",
